# Try the people endpoints by hand, using VS Code's REST Client extension or Visual Studio.
#
# They need an access token for a Family.Admin, read from a git-ignored file so it never
# sits in this tracked file (this repo is public):
#
#   1. Sign in to the web app, open the browser's dev tools, go to Network, click the `me`
#      request, and copy the value after "Bearer " in its Authorization header.
#   2. Put it in src/FamilyTree.Api/.env, next to this file, as one line:
#      FAMILYTREE_TOKEN=<the token>
#
# It lasts about an hour. Use fictional people here for now.

#@api = http://localhost:5080
@api = https://api.family.andrewmacleod.com
@token = {{$dotenv FAMILYTREE_TOKEN}}

### Add a person
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sex": "Female",
  "names": [
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "Campbell", "type": "Birth" },
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "MacLeod", "type": "Married" }
  ]
}

### Add someone who shares a name with an existing person. Without allowDuplicate this gets 409, listing the matches.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people?allowDuplicate=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": [{ "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "MacLeod" }] }

### List people, a page at a time
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people?skip=0&take=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one person: replace the ID with one from the list
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/01a191bb-71f7-7816-930b-25f3daecd1a9
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a person, with their names and events. This can't be undone: replace the ID with care
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Record a birth: replace the ID. Dates can be as fuzzy as the records: abt 1870, bef Mar 1901, 1870-75, Q2 1880
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/events
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Birth", "date": "abt 1870", "place": "Innellan, Argyll" }

### Change a person: replace the ID. This replaces their sex and all their names, so send everything to keep.
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sex": "Female",
  "names": [
    { "givenName": "Morag", "surname": "MacLeod", "type": "Birth" }
  ]
}

### Change when and where an event happened: person ID, then event ID. Its type stays the same.
PUT {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/events/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "date": "bef 1871",
  "place": "Innellan, Argyll"
}

### Remove an event: person ID, then event ID.
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/events/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Record a family: replace the IDs. Leave out partner2Id if the other parent is unknown.
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/families
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "partner1Id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "partner2Id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "type": "Marriage"
}

### Add a child to a family. Relationships: Biological, Adopted, Step, Foster, Presumed, Unknown
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/families/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/children
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "childId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "partner1Relationship": "Biological",
  "partner2Relationship": "Step"
}

### A person's families, as a child and as a partner
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/families
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Take a child out of a family: family ID, then child ID. The person isn't deleted.
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/admin/families/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/children/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a family and its child links. The people aren't deleted.
DELETE {{api}}/api/v1/admin/families/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refused: a person needs a given name
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": [{ "surname": "MacLeod" }] }
